# All optional — every value below has a sensible default.
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and uncomment any line you want to override.

# Directory containing your Claude Code transcripts (*.jsonl).
# Default: ~/.claude/projects
# CLAUDE_PROJECTS_DIR=/path/to/.claude/projects

# --- Parse cache (lib/usage-cache.ts) ---

# Directory for the persistent parse-cache index file
# (usage-index.json). Default: ./.cache next to the project.
# USAGE_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/cache/dir

# Set to "off" to disable the ON-DISK cache file only — no
# .cache/usage-index.json is read or written. Parsed transcripts are still
# kept in memory and swept incrementally (only new bytes reparsed) for the
# life of the process; a restart just always starts cold since there's no
# file to reload from. This is NOT "always full reparse" — use
# /api/usage?rebuild=1 for that. Any other value (or unset) leaves the
# on-disk cache on.
# USAGE_CACHE=off

# --- Chat panel (optional) ---
# The Overview chat panel talks to a local LM Studio OpenAI-compatible server.
# If LM Studio isn't running, only the chat panel is affected — the rest of the
# dashboard works normally.

# LM Studio base URL.
# Default: http://localhost:1234/v1
# LM_STUDIO_URL=http://localhost:1234/v1

# Model id to chat with — must match a model loaded in LM Studio.
# Default: google/gemma-4-e4b
# LM_STUDIO_MODEL=google/gemma-4-e4b
